# Vendored blamejs — treat as immutable + binary-safe. The vendor
# manifest pins versions; CRLF/LF conversion between Windows and
# Linux checkouts must never touch the vendored tree (it ships the
# noble-post-quantum bundle with embedded base64 + other byte-sensitive
# data that would corrupt under line-ending rewrites).
lib/vendor/** -text binary

# Shell scripts MUST stay LF — they run inside Linux CI / container
# steps where bash chokes on CRLF with "$'\r': command not found".
*.sh text eol=lf

# Derived artifacts the release-notes generator owns end-to-end —
# rebuild emits LF, so pin LF here too. Without this, Windows
# checkouts get CRLF and the `--check` drift gate in smoke would have
# to keep eating the cost of normalizing both sides.
CHANGELOG.md text eol=lf
release-notes/*.json text eol=lf

# Native modules — always binary.
*.node binary
*.so binary
*.dylib binary
*.dll binary
*.a binary

# Standard binary types.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.tar binary
*.tgz binary
*.pdf binary
